---
// The Holder mark of the Community chat (docs/contracts/phase-6-holders-2.md, section 2.1): the word
// "Holder" beside a writer's short address, in the shape of the admin's mark and quieter than it. It has no
// drawn mark, because only an admin's message carries the mark of Prix, and no figure: never a level, an
// amount or a tick. Its label tells assistive technology what it means.
//
// Whether a message carries it is the server's `holder`, read from the writer's stored token row, and
// never something this page works out. It changes no order, no count and no other style of the row.
import { text } from '../../../content/index.ts';
---

<span class="room-holder">
  <span aria-hidden="true">{text('social.roomHolderMark', 'Holder')}</span>
  <span class="visually-hidden">{text('social.roomHolderMarkLabel', 'This wallet holds $PRIX, as Prix last read it.')}</span>
</span>

<style>
  /*
    The admin's mark has a ring of the chosen ink, the wash and the drawn mark, in the ink at a strong weight;
    this one is metadata beside the address, never a badge (DC-H2-2): the address's grey at the regular
    weight in both themes, no fill, and only the hairline of the line colour around it, in the same size,
    padding and corner as the admin's. The dark theme's quiet ink is the ink itself, so it is not used here:
    a second white pill would weaken the one cue that a message is Prix's.
  */
  .room-holder {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex: none;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 var(--rule-hair) var(--line);
    color: var(--grey);
    font-size: var(--text-12);
    font-weight: var(--weight-regular);
    line-height: var(--leading-12);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
